SUMMARY:On The Sea @ Merlin Falmouth
DESCRIPTION:On The Sea (1h 55min)\n★★★★☆\nDrama\, Romance\n\nJack has been 
 married to Maggie for over half his life. He works as a Hand Raker on the 
 mussel beds in North Wales alongside his younger brother\, Dyfan\, and Dyf
 an’s three sons. Jack has always assumed that his own boy\, Tom\, will joi
 n the family business on leaving school but Tom’s resistance to follow in 
 his footsteps creates familial tension. Tensions are further inflamed by t
 he arrival of an itinerant deckhand\, Daniel\, who makes known his feeling
 s for Jack. In this remote\, rural community where life revolves around Ch
 urch and fishery\, Jack is faced with an impossible dilemma. On The Sea is
  a beautiful\, sensual and at times\, tragic exploration of masculinity\, 
 place and desire.\n\nStarring: Barry Ward\, Lorne MacFadyen\, Liz White\, 
 Henry Lawfull\, Celyn Jones\, Leisa Gwenllian\n\nFilm release at Merlin Ci
 nemas Falmouth\nBook tickets: /film/on-the-sea\n\nFilm details: https://ev
 enwebb.github.io/merlin-cinemas/films/on-the-sea.html
LOCATION:Merlin Cinemas Falmouth
URL:/film/on-the-sea
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
